From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:51:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pci: brcmstb: leave the BCM2712 RP1 link to the firmware and
 Linux

On Raspberry Pi 5 and CM5 one BCM2712 PCIe controller's endpoint is RP1,
the I/O chip behind Ethernet, USB and GPIO. The Pi firmware brings it up
and Linux drives it; U-Boot has no RP1 driver. Enumerating that link and
asserting PERST on it again before booting the OS left RP1 unusable to
Linux: "BAR 0 ... not claimed; can't enable device", rp1 probe -22, and
no Ethernet or USB. The device tree marks that controller with the rp1
node: do not bind it, and enumerate the other controllers as before.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
 drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c b/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c
index 5c4366c306d..49f0cb4e118 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie_brcmstb.c
@@ -556,6 +556,24 @@ static int brcm_pcie_post_setup_bcm2712(struct brcm_pcie *pcie)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * On BCM2712 (Raspberry Pi 5, CM5) one controller's endpoint is RP1, the I/O
+ * chip behind Ethernet, USB and GPIO. The Pi firmware brings RP1 up and Linux
+ * drives it; U-Boot has no RP1 driver. Enumerating that link and asserting
+ * PERST on it again before booting the OS (remove, DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE) leaves
+ * RP1 unusable to Linux: "BAR 0 ... not claimed; can't enable device", rp1
+ * probe -22, and no Ethernet or USB. The device tree marks that controller
+ * with the rp1 node, so do not bind it; the other controllers (the M.2 slot)
+ * are enumerated as before.
+ */
+static int brcm_pcie_bind(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	if (ofnode_valid(dev_read_subnode(dev, "rp1")))
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int brcm_pcie_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 {
 	struct udevice *ctlr = pci_get_controller(dev);
@@ -840,6 +858,7 @@ U_BOOT_DRIVER(pcie_brcm_base) = {
 	.id			= UCLASS_PCI,
 	.ops			= &brcm_pcie_ops,
 	.of_match		= brcm_pcie_ids,
+	.bind			= brcm_pcie_bind,
 	.probe			= brcm_pcie_probe,
 	.remove			= brcm_pcie_remove,
 	.of_to_plat	= brcm_pcie_of_to_plat,
